    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3aa01c1259574683b7b72b23ac0d015c",
      "statement": "Re-verification covers ALL in-scope bindings on every open: for each, the chosen account's verifier is resolved via clientUser.getVerifier(accountId, vendorId) (null when disconnected, vendor mismatch throws) and handed to the gatekeeper facet's addObserver, run concurrently so Cap'n Web batches, with every failure collected rather than just the first.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/overseer.ts#L7959-L7994",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a053877ef17661837a644428dfd0d767e7950c1a3b6915cded0399f584dbc07d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dd56374a5640414ba11c3bbd397363fa",
      "statement": "Verification failures drop the failed account choices and offer one bounded re-prompt (MAX_CONFIG_REPROMPTS = 1) with the failure reason attached so the client can aim re-authentication at the right account; after the budget the open is denied with a terminal error naming each failed connection and account — treating every failure as repairable rather than distinguishing denial from outage.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/overseer.ts#L7996-L8020",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c1efa5ff447aca01ac33717a738c88cf8d063f924ae3f2700129ece3fb77743:"
