        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_36515385c5094761a3f4804f1ea7e2f2",
      "statement": "The observer record is persisted ONLY after all addObserver calls succeed — that is the canonical moment the user becomes a configured observer — and a failure rolls back by removing only observers registered during this call, leaving pre-existing registrations intact because removing one would break excludeObservers while the persisted record still asserts it exists.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/overseer.ts#L8025-L8034",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f457d74596b1af9c1eb70f4c9603cf06740749ea08e52fdbe997610e22cf42c5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ce553c62dcd64dfa86974153c186440e",
      "statement": "Re-verification at every open is intentional: it catches revocation of the user's underlying resource access at their next open, and gatekeepers for which re-running addObserver is expensive should implement their own caching strategy — the performance/immediacy tradeoff is each gatekeeper's to choose.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/observers.md#L295-L302",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c6d97fbfa45de7df7f173aa1f1b312428f26d51d5405d71bb630b9b69b779f2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_abd8d2350d1c4ef2adf20836be713ba2",
      "statement": "Forward exclusion: an observation naming excludeObservers proceeds only if every named observer has already lost access in the sharing graph (their observer records are then torn down); if any named observer is still authorized the observation is blocked — so erring toward naming an observer is never a leak, at worst it blocks an observation that could have been allowed, and the leak-relevant gate is always the live sharing graph.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.agents/skills/write-gatekeeper/SKILL.md#L293-L295",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:490412eedbb3f1f737db462cbab9bb6f39a5e72c276793cb98dd14bc47308976:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/overseer.ts#L4558-L4615",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a83a5f46f78f49b7d57a0d0b7aa2351e490cdb449364a399e74d285a680da32f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d2270ec801a34105845a1bacbdb40403",
      "statement": "Verifiers: the observer's own connected account mints an opaque GatekeeperUserVerifier which the overseer passes back ONLY to the same vendor that minted it, making the vendor's cast to its own extended verifier interface safe — e.g. GitHub's hasRepoAccess queries with the observer's own token where a 404 on the repo means no access.",
